{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Init.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.SigmaJGeometricCarrier","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HodgeWeilRealStructure"],"declarations":25,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.FGal_fixed_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.FGal_fixed_iff","kind":"theorem","line":220,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.lean#L220-L236","doc":"**`Fix(F) = {(a, a)}` — the Galois fixed locus is the diagonal**, NOT the real\nform `{(w, w̄)}`. A vector is `F`-fixed iff its two Hodge parts are equal. This\ndistinguishes the two real structures at the level of fixed loci: `c`-fixed means\n`H^{0,1} = conj(H^{1,0})` (`c_fixed_iff_real_form`); `F`-fixed means\n`H^{0,1} = H^{1,0}`. Different subspaces — the antilinear/linear distinction has\nfixed-locus content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.c_fixed_iff_real_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.c_fixed_iff_real_form","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.lean#L204-L218","doc":"**`Fix(c) = {(w, w̄)}` — the complete real-form characterization.** A vector is\n`c`-fixed iff its `H^{0,1}` part is the conjugate of its `H^{1,0}` part. The\nexisting `c_fixes_real_form` proved only `⊇` (every `(w, w̄)` is fixed); this is\nthe iff, so `Fix(c)` is *exactly* the Weil real form `H¹(ℝ)`, `dim_ℝ = 8`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.c_swaps_hodge_other","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.c_swaps_hodge_other","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.lean#L196-L202","doc":"**`c` swaps the OTHER Hodge piece** — `c(0, b) = (b̄, 0)`: maps `H^{0,1}`\n(first slot zero) into `H^{1,0}` (second slot zero). Completes `c_swaps_hodge`\n(which handled `H^{1,0} → H^{0,1}`); together they show `c` interchanges the two\npieces both ways. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.weil_galois_compose","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.weil_galois_compose","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.lean#L186-L194","doc":"**`c ∘ F = F ∘ c = conjV`** — the Weil real structure and the Galois real\nstructure differ exactly by complex conjugation (the standard `c = conj ∘ F`\nrelation for a real variety). Both compositions strip the `SWAP` and leave pure\ncoordinate conjugation. This is what makes the antilinear `c`, not the linear\n`F`, the Hodge conjugation: they are conjugate-related, not equal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.conjV_antilinear","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.conjV_antilinear","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.lean#L177-L184","doc":"`conjV` is antilinear — `conjV(λ·v) = λ̄·conjV(v)` (uses `conj_mul`). Together\nwith `conjV_involutive` this makes `conjV` an antilinear involution like `c`, but\none that does NOT swap the Hodge pieces (it is `c ∘ F`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.conjV_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.conjV_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.lean#L171-L175","doc":"`conjV` (whole-`H¹` complex conjugation) is an involution — it is the third\nreal structure, `c ∘ F = F ∘ c` (see `weil_galois_compose`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.unitExp_recovers_bar_exchange","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.unitExp_recovers_bar_exchange","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.lean#L161-L167","doc":"Bridge to the degenerate-locus shadow (`SigmaJGeometricCarrier`): the nome's\nvalue at exponent `1` is `q = i` and at exponent `3` is `q = −i`, and negating the\nexponent of `q = i` recovers the bar exchange `q = i ↦ q = −i`\n(`bar_exchanges_degenerate_pair` is the `n = z1` case of `unitExp_neg_eq_conj`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.unitExp_channelSwap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.unitExp_channelSwap","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.lean#L153-L159","doc":"**`τ ↦ ½ − τ` ↔ `q ↦ −q⁻¹ = −q̄`.** The channel-swap half-shift `z2 + (−τ)`\nmaps to `−conj(e(τ))`. Note it FIXES the degenerate pair (`n = z1 ↦ z1`,\n`n = z3 ↦ z3`): the exponent-level refinement of\n`SigmaJGeometricCarrier.transpose_fixes_degenerate_pair`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.unitExp_neg_eq_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.unitExp_neg_eq_conj","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.lean#L145-L151","doc":"**`τ ↦ −τ` ↔ `q ↦ q⁻¹ = q̄`.** Exponent negation is nome conjugation:\n`e(−τ) = conj(e(τ))` for every exponent (on the unit circle `q⁻¹ = q̄`). This is\naudit §2's `τ(q̄) = −conj(τ(q))` read as an exponent-group identity — automatic,\nmoduli-independent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.unitExp_distinct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.unitExp_distinct","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.lean#L137-L143","doc":"**`unitExp` is faithful** — the four nome values are pairwise distinct, so the\nhomomorphism is injective onto the units (the exponent group law is non-vacuous\ncontent, not a collapse). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.unitExp_add_eq_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.unitExp_add_eq_mul","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.lean#L130-L135","doc":"**`unitExp` is a group homomorphism** `e(a+b) = e(a)·e(b)`: the nome turns\nexponent addition into unit multiplication. (16-case `decide`; breaks under any\nmis-assignment of the four roots.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.unitExp_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.unitExp_half","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.lean#L126-L128","doc":"The half-period value `e(2) = −1` (`unitExp z2` is the order-2 element — the\n`½`-shift that realizes the channel swap below). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.unitExp_values","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.unitExp_values","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.lean#L121-L124","doc":"The four nome values, pinned. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.unitExp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.unitExp","kind":"def","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.lean#L112-L119","doc":"**The nome `q = e^{2πiτ}` on the degenerate stratum**, as a map from the\nexponent group to the Gaussian units: `e(0)=1`, `e(1)=i`, `e(2)=−1`, `e(3)=−i`\n(the fourth roots of unity `i^n`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.Z4.neg_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.Z4.neg_neg","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.lean#L107-L108","doc":"`−(−τ) = τ`: exponent negation is an involution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.Z4.neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.Z4.neg","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.lean#L102-L105","doc":"Exponent negation `τ ↦ −τ` (the involution the bar/inversion `q ↦ q⁻¹`\nlifts to). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.Z4.add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.Z4.add","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.lean#L95-L100","doc":"Exponent addition (mod 4) — the additive group law `τ + τ'`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.instReprZ4.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.instReprZ4.repr","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.lean#L91-L91","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.instReprZ4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.instReprZ4","kind":"instance","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.lean#L91-L91","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.instDecidableEqZ4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.instDecidableEqZ4","kind":"instance","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.lean#L91-L91","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.Z4.z3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.Z4.z3","kind":"ctor","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.lean#L90-L90","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.Z4.z2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.Z4.z2","kind":"ctor","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.lean#L90-L90","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.Z4.z1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.Z4.z1","kind":"ctor","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.lean#L90-L90","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.Z4.z0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.Z4.z0","kind":"ctor","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.lean#L90-L90","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.Z4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.Z4","kind":"inductive","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/B2LiftAutomaticIngredients.lean#L86-L91","doc":"The quarter-period exponent lattice `ℤ/4ℤ` — the group of nome exponents `τ`\nmodulo the period, on the degenerate stratum where `q ∈ {1, i, −1, −i}`. Lean-core\ninductive (no Mathlib `ZMod`), so every law below is `decide`/`rfl`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}